From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:42:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] feat(shader): prove a first-lane T# offset through
 waterfall loop masks

A T# loaded with s_load_dwordx8 from a user-data table at an offset taken
from v_readfirstlane inside a waterfall loop stopped with "GetImageResource
dword 0 is not a valid runtime value". The offset is the first active lane
of a VGPR the shader set only in some lanes, so its value is a select of
the lane's index and an old value, and the table column reads it as the
index only when the read's active mask implies the select's condition.
That proof followed LogicalAnd and nothing else; a waterfall loop's mask
is a Phi of the entry mask and the lanes still to do, and a mask restored
from a saved EXEC is the lane's bit of a ballot.

ActiveMaskSelects, now used wherever a select under a first-lane mask is
resolved to its active arm (table columns, the SRT validator, evaluator
and tape), also proves the implication through:

- LogicalAnd, LogicalOr, LogicalNot and SelectU1 on either side, and Phis
  and selects whose selector is a constant;
- mask Phis, by induction over their loop, used only when the condition
  is defined before the loop;
- the lane bit of a saved EXEC or VCC word made of ballots, ANDs, ORs and
  complements (wave32, and both halves of wave64), and the condition's
  own lane bit of the same word.

Each query memoizes its steps and gives up after 2^20 of them or 24 Phis
deep. ActiveMaskImplies, which the evaluators ask of every Bool value
under a mask, keeps its LogicalAnd-only proof: the full one there made a
compile take minutes.

Offline (no guest memory, under Wine), 100 of the 128 compute shaders of
a retail title that stopped so now compile, and all 100 validate. The
other 28 still stop there; those looked at need a lane mask loaded from
memory, or a proof that relates a mask and a condition edge by edge
across a merge (pairing the Phis of one block was tried: it did not
settle them, and made some compiles take minutes). The largest of the
100 take up to two minutes each.

Tested: tests/DescriptorSelectionTests.cpp compiles a waterfall loop that
loads a T# per lane from a user-data table; it stops with the old error
without the change and binds an image table with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
