+# shader
+
+## change [Image table pointer indexing]
+
+- [Image table pointer indexing](../../../core/shader/recompiler/Optimization/src/ResourceTracker.cpp) propagates 32-bit value bounds through `ReadFirstLane` and `SelectU32` so waterfall key masks keep their bit domain. A first-lane offset's select is resolved only where the read's active mask [provably implies](../../../core/shader/recompiler/Optimization/src/SrtWalker/SrtInstructionPredicates.cpp) its condition; a mask loaded from memory, or a proof past 2^20 steps or 48 Phis, still refuses the T#. The proof assumes a ballot holds every live lane's bit, and that unselected inactive lanes need not be uniform across the full wave. The same assumption lets the two `s_load`s of one T# record match when one offset is added before `v_readfirstlane` and the other after (`ReadFirstLane(Select(mask, (key << 5) + 16, old), mask)` against `ReadFirstLane(key, mask) << 5`): with no active lane the hardware reads lane 0 of the inactive arm, and the table still binds the whole record.
-- 
